  "transcription": "Declassified in Part - Sanitized Copy Approved for Release 2011/12/06 : CIA-RDP89B01330R000300510007-2\nSECRET\n25X1\n25X1\nCBW Future Monitoring Capabilities:\n• On 9 November, we met with [illegible] to introduce our thinking, as represented in the 12 October discussion paper, on the need to establish a CIPC working group to undertake a comprehensive, systematic review of ways to enhance the Intelligence Community capability to monitor Soviet capabilities for chemical, biological and toxin warfare.\n• Both [illegible] fully endorsed the concept, sharing our concern over the need to sustain momentum in this area long enough to achieve meaningful progress across a multitasking front. They promised to look over the discussion paper and provide critical comments quickly. The STAP initiative on improving analytical reaction time in the event of future Soviet use, as in Afghanistan and SEA, was briefly discussed. They agreed that, although this was important, it was only one piece of a much more fundamental gap in extant intelligence capabilities.\n\nEast Germany; Intelligence Information Needs:\n• [illegible] visited [illegible] DDI, on Friday to explore the potential for an East Germany study. [illegible] would support a study on East Germany and sees a persistent intelligence gap relating to /Internal Political Dynamics/. He would also like to see the study expanded beyond East Germany to the northern tier of Eastern Europe. [illegible] has meetings scheduled for later this week with State/INR and DIA/DB personnel to further explore this subject.",
