  "transcription": "TOP SECRET CHESS RUFF\nApproved For Release 2001/08/21 : CIA-RDP78B04560A000200010048-4\n\n25X1A KRAASNOYARSK STATIC TEST STAND 5605N 09327E\nIDENTIFICATION ONLY.\n\n25X1D\n\n25X1A SEVERODVINSK (MOLOTOVSK) SHIPYARD 402 6434N 03949E\n\nNO APPARENT CHANGE IN FACILITIES SINCE EXCEPT ONE ADDITIONAL POSSIBLE PONTOON PIER AT NAVAL BASE. AT LEAST 10 VESSELS ARE EVIDENT BUT SMALL SCALE AND POOR IMAGE QUALITY PRECLUDE ACCURATE COUNT AND IDENTIFICATION OF VESSELS, OR ESTIMATION OF PERCENTAGE OF YARD DEVOTED TO SHIP CONSTRUCTION.\n\n25X1D\n\n25X1A LENINGRAD SUSPECT ABM AREA 5955N 03020E\nA SEARCH WITHIN A 40 NM RADIUS OF LENINGRAD REVEALED NO NEW RADAR SITES. NO APPARENT CHANGE IN THE PADDLEWHEEL SITES LOCATED 16 NM NE 32 NM SW AND 35 NM NW OF LENINGRAD. SEARCH AREA IS 70 PERCENT CLOUD FREE.\n\n25X1D\n\nBONUS 1. MARINA GORKA MRBM LAUNCH SITE 5326N 02745E\nNEWLY-IDENTIFIED INLINE MRBM LAUNCH SITE LOCATED 15.3 NM WSW OF MARINA GORKA AT 53-26-15N 027-45-25E CONSISTS OF 4 LAUNCH PADS ALIGNED IN A SW DIRECTION. SITE IS PROBABLY COMPLETE. CLOUDS COVER PROBABLE LOCATION OF SUPPORT AREA.\n\n25X1D\n\nBONUS 2. LENINGRAD SA-3 SAM SITE 6001N 02941E\n\n7\nApproved For Release 2001/08/21 : CIA-RDP78B04560A000200010048-4\nTOP SECRET CHESS RUFF",
